# The sensors HAL creates the lid switch as a uinput device, and was denied.
#
#   E sensors-hal: mot_flip:122, mot_flip: failed to open uinput: Permission denied
#   avc: denied { write } for comm="android.hardwar" name="uinput" dev="tmpfs"
#        scontext=u:r:hal_sensors_default:s0 tcontext=u:object_r:uhid_device:s0
#        tclass=chr_file permissive=0
#
# That is the BINDING constraint on this device's fold logic, not the hinge
# sensor. MotFlip_LID (SW_LID) is a uinput node the HAL creates; denied, it never
# appears, and EventHub's whole inventory is gpio-keys, pmic_pwrkey, pmic_resin,
# double-tap, s-double-tap, gdx_cli_0, goodix_ts -- no lid.
#
# EVERY one of the seven states in fold/device_state_configuration.xml carries a
# <lid-switch> condition, and DeviceStateProviderImpl's LidSwitchBooleanSupplier
# throws IllegalStateException("Have not received lid switch value") while
# mIsLidOpen is null, so the state is skipped. States 1-5 are additionally hard
# false because com.motorola.sensor.hinge_posture is missing. Result:
#   DeviceStateProviderImpl: No declared device states match any of the required conditions
#   DeviceStateManagerService: Cannot notify device state info change before the
#                              initial state has been committed
# and the device state stays INVALID (= STATE_DEFAULT = -1), so
# display_layout_configuration.xml is parsed but NEVER APPLIED.
#
# With this rule, and even with the hinge sensor still broken, the provider falls
# through states 1-5 and lands on state 6 OPENED_HALL (lid-only, evaluated last):
# inner primary, outer disabled -- the correct open-device behaviour.
allow hal_sensors_default uhid_device:chr_file rw_file_perms;

# vendor.camera.led.torchmode, moved off vendor_default_prop by property.te so
# that the camera provider can set it at all. THIS GRANT IS THE OTHER HALF OF
# THAT CHANGE, not a new capability: sensors.qsh.so is one of only two binaries
# in the firmware that reference the string, and before the relabel it read the
# property for free through the blanket domain.te:508 vendor_default_prop grant.
# Without this the sensors HAL silently loses a read it has today.
#
# `set` as well as `get` because that is what stock gives it
# (vendor_sepolicy.cil:14108-14109), not because a write was observed here.
set_prop(hal_sensors_default, vendor_camera_ledtorchmode_prop)
